## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design edge-optimized streaming PCA with strict resource limits and actionable, interpretable alerts.

## Key Concepts

- Streaming PCA with randomized SVD
- Incremental imputation for missing data
- Drift detection on loadings for nonstationarity
- On-device latency/memory budgeting
- Interpretability of loadings for governance alerts

## Code Example

```javascript
// pseudo-code: streaming PCA update
function streamPCAStep(row, state) {
  const imputed = impute(row, state.imputer);
  const projected = project(imputed, state.components);
  state = updateSVD(state, projected);
  return state;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you validate drift thresholds in production?
- How would you balance on-device explainability with privacy constraints?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design a beginner PCA pipeline in a cross-tenant setting with latency constraints and interpret loadings for cohort definitions. Emphasizes data cleaning, scaling, component retention strategy, and practical mapping from components to business actions.

## Key Concepts
- PCA basics: imputation, scaling, centering
- Global vs per-tenant PCA; explained variance threshold
- Loadings interpretation; cohort definition
- Latency considerations: batch vs streaming; incremental options

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudocode illustrating preprocessing and PCA call
function buildPCA(data) {
  const imputed = imputeMeanPerFeature(data);
  const scaled = scaleToUnitVariance(imputed);
  // assume PCA is available and returns components/loadings
  const pca = new PCA(scaled, {nComponents: 6});
  return pca.loadings;
}
```

```javascript
// Example interpretation
const top = pcaLoadings[0];
console.log(top); // { sessions_per_week: 0.68, content_views: 0.52, ... }
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you monitor stability of the 6 components across weeks?
- How would you adjust if the explained variance dips below the target over time?

## Why This Is Asked
Explores federated, incremental PCA in production with privacy and latency constraints.

## Key Concepts
- Federated incremental PCA
- Sufficient statistics aggregation
- Exponential forgetting for nonstationarity
- Drift detection via loadings/explained variance
- Edge imputation and synchronization

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo: local update with forgetting
let cov = 0, mean = 0, alpha = 0.98; // forgetting
for (let x of stream) {
  let d = x - mean;
  cov = alpha * cov + (1 - alpha) * d * d;
  mean = alpha * mean + (1 - alpha) * x;
}
// Server: aggregate covariances
let globalCov = sum_i(w_i * cov_i);
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate drift vs seasonal pattern and adjust components?
- What happens when device connectivity is intermittent and how would you adapt the protocol?

Why This Is Asked
Assesses edge deployment thinking: PCA under tight latency, memory, and drift, plus concrete handling of missing data and scaling.

Key Concepts
- On-device PCA projection and memory constraints
- Simple imputation and feature scaling in embedded environments
- Component retention criteria (variance explained, elbow)
- Drift monitoring and offline/online update strategies

Code Example
```javascript
// x: length-16 feature vector
// W: 4x16 projection matrix stored on device
function project(x, W){
  const y = new Array(4).fill(0);
  for(let i=0;i<4;i++){
    let s=0;
    for(let j=0;j<16;j++) s += W[i][j]*x[j];
    y[i] = s;
  }
  return y;
}
```

Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate latency on-device?
- How would you handle new sensors or distribution shifts?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical use of online PCA with drift in a realtime setting, plus realistic preprocessing and maintenance decisions. It checks which components to keep, when to retrain, and how latency shapes choices.

## Key Concepts
- IncrementalPCA for streaming data
- Imputation and scaling in a tight loop
- Explained_variance_ratio for component budgeting
- Drift detection and retraining triggers under latency constraints

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudocode: update loop for streaming features
let pca = new IncrementalPCA({nComponents: k});
for (chunk of stream) {
  let X = imputeAndScale(chunk); //  // mean impute + scale
  pca.partialFit(X);
  let Z = pca.transform(X);
  detector.predict(Z);
  monitorDrift(pca.explainedVarianceRatio_, pca.components_);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you set drift thresholds and trigger retraining?
- How do you handle feature addition/removal over time and maintain a stable k?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests end-to-end PCA thinking under real-time, multi-tenant constraints with practical privacy and latency trade-offs.

## Key Concepts
- Incremental PCA for streaming data
- Per-tenant preprocessing and privacy
- Loadings-to-alert mappings and latency budgeting

## Code Example
```javascript
// simple scoring skeleton
function score(pcaScores, loadings, threshold){
  const alerts = [];
  for(const i in pcaScores){
    if(Math.abs(pcaScores[i])>threshold) alerts.push(i);
  }
  return alerts;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you monitor drift in component loadings over time?
- How would you calibrate thresholds to maintain a target false-positive rate?
